# 低频词汇 List10
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2026恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List10核心词汇

reclaim /rɪˈkleɪm/ v. 收回 The government reclaimed the land for public use. 政府收回了土地用于公共用途。
rectify /ˈrektɪfaɪ/ v. 纠正 The company took steps to rectify the error. 公司采取措施纠正了错误。
recur /rɪˈkɜː(ː)r/ v. 复发 The problem continues to recur despite treatment. 尽管进行了治疗，问题仍然复发。
redundant /rɪˈdʌndənt/ adj. 多余的 The new system made many manual processes redundant. 新系统使许多手工流程变得多余。
reign /reɪn/ n./v. 统治 The monarch's reign lasted for decades. 君主的统治持续了几十年。
reminiscent /ˌremɪˈnɪsnt/ adj. 令人回忆的 The scene was reminiscent of a bygone era. 这个场景让人回忆起过去的时代。
renounce /rɪˈnaʊns/ v. 放弃 He renounced his claim to the throne. 他放弃了王位继承权。
repeal /rɪˈpiːl/ v. 废除 The law was repealed after widespread protests. 法律在广泛抗议后被废除。
repel /rɪˈpel/ v. 击退；排斥 The army repelled the enemy attack. 军队击退了敌人的进攻。
reproach /rɪˈprəʊtʃ/ v./n. 责备 She reproached herself for not speaking up. 她责备自己没有说出来。
resemble /rɪˈzembl/ v. 像 The new building resembles a ship. 新建筑像一艘船。
reside /rɪˈzaɪd/ v. 存在 The problem resides in the lack of funding. 问题在于缺乏资金。
resign /rɪˈzaɪn/ v. 顺从 She resigned herself to the fact that change would be slow. 她接受了变化会很缓慢的事实。
resilient /rɪˈzɪliənt/ adj. 有恢复力的 The community proved resilient in the face of disaster. 社区在灾难面前证明了自己的韧性。
retaliate /rɪˈtælieɪt/ v. 报复 The country retaliated with trade sanctions. 该国以贸易制裁进行报复。
retrieve /rɪˈtriːv/ v. 取回 The dog retrieved the ball from the water. 狗从水中取回了球。
rigid /ˈrɪdʒɪd/ adj. 严格的 The curriculum is too rigid to allow creativity. 课程过于严格，不允许创造力。
robust /rəˈbʌst/ adj. 强健的 The debate was robust but constructive. 辩论激烈但具有建设性。
safeguard /ˈseɪfɡɑːd/ v./n. 保障 The constitution safeguards individual rights. 宪法保障个人权利。
saturate /ˈsætʃəreɪt/ v. 使饱和 The market is saturated with similar products. 市场上充斥着类似产品。
segregate /ˈseɡrɪɡeɪt/ v. 隔离 The policy segregated students by ability. 该政策按能力将学生分开。
shatter /ˈʃætə(r)/ v. 粉碎 The scandal shattered public confidence. 丑闻粉碎了公众信心。
sheer /ʃɪə(r)/ adj. 纯粹的 The sheer scale of the project is impressive. 该项目的纯粹规模令人印象深刻。
shrewd /ʃruːd/ adj. 精明的 She is a shrewd businesswoman. 她是一位精明的女商人。
skeptical /ˈskeptɪkl/ adj. 怀疑的 Investors remain skeptical about the recovery. 投资者对复苏仍持怀疑态度。
soar /sɔː(r)/ v. 猛增 Prices have soared in recent months. 近几个月来价格猛增。
sovereign /ˈsɒvrɪn/ adj./n. 主权的 Every sovereign nation has the right to self-determination. 每个主权国家都有自决权。
spontaneous /spɒnˈteɪniəs/ adj. 自发的 The celebration was a spontaneous expression of joy. 庆祝是自发的喜悦表达。
stagnant /ˈstæɡnənt/ adj. 停滞的 The economy remained stagnant for years. 经济多年来一直停滞不前。
stern /stɜːn/ adj. 严厉的 The government took stern measures against corruption. 政府对腐败采取了严厉措施。
